<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tinchebray" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tinchebray.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-28">28 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Henry I of England defeats and captures Robert Curthose at Tinchebray</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In Normandy, King Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> defeated the Norman army of his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a>, Duke of Normandy, and captured him. Robert spent the rest of his life in captivity, and Henry reunited Normandy with England.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tinchebray">Battle of Tinchebray</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
